---
title: "Case study hero"
eyebrow: "Components"
lead: "The opening of a case study page: a back button, an eyebrow, a title, a subtitle, optional buttons and a 16:9 image."
permalink: /components/case-study-hero/
---
{% from "components.njk" import button %}
<section aria-labelledby="demo-h">
  <h2 id="demo-h" class="type-h2">Case study hero</h2>
  <p>The hero sits on the page surface. A tertiary back button comes first, then a band with the text on the left and the image on the right. The text has an eyebrow, the page's one <code>h1</code>, a subtitle and up to a few secondary buttons that open in a new tab. The image is 16:9. The text and image below are placeholders.</p>
  {% demo "Case study hero with placeholder text and a placeholder image", "block" %}
  <header class="cs-hero">
    <div class="cs-hero__back">
      {{ button("All work", type="tertiary", href="#", icon="arrow_back", iconPosition="leading") }}
    </div>
    <div class="cs-hero__band">
      <div class="cs-hero__text">
        <div class="cs-hero__heading">
          <p class="cs-hero__eyebrow type-label">Project type, Role</p>
          <p class="cs-hero__title type-h1">Case study title</p>
        </div>
        <div class="cs-hero__lede">
          <p class="cs-hero__subtitle type-lead">One or two sentences that say what the project was and what changed.</p>
          <div class="cs-hero__actions">
            {{ button("Link label", type="secondary", href="#", icon="open_in_new", iconPosition="trailing", external=true) }}
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
      <div class="cs-hero__image">
        <div class="placeholder-image"><p class="type-small">Placeholder image, 16:9</p></div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>
  {% enddemo %}
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="layout-h">
  <h2 id="layout-h" class="type-h2">Layout and spacing</h2>
  <div class="table-wrap" tabindex="0" role="region" aria-label="Case study hero layout by breakpoint, scrollable">
    <table class="docs-table type-small">
      <thead><tr><th scope="col">Breakpoint</th><th scope="col">Layout</th><th scope="col">Band padding above and below</th><th scope="col">Gap between text and image</th><th scope="col">Gap inside the text</th></tr></thead>
      <tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row">Mobile</th><td>Text, then the image full width</td><td>32px</td><td>24px</td><td>32px</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Tablet (768px up)</th><td>Text, then the image full width</td><td>48px</td><td>32px</td><td>40px</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row">Desktop (1024px up)</th><td>12 columns: text in columns 1 to 6, image in columns 7 to 12</td><td>64px</td><td>24px (column gap)</td><td>32px, with the eyebrow and title at the top and the subtitle at the bottom</td></tr>
      </tbody>
    </table>
  </div>
  <p>The sides use the page padding, so the text lines up with the header. The back row is 8px above and below on mobile and 16px from 768px up. The back button is pulled left by 12px so its arrow lines up with the grid and not with the button's own inset. The eyebrow and title are 16px apart, and the subtitle and buttons are 24px apart. The buttons stack at full width on mobile and sit in a row from 768px up, 16px apart.</p>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="color-h">
  <h2 id="color-h" class="type-h2">Color</h2>
  <p>The hero sits on <code>surface/neutral/base</code>. The eyebrow is <code>text/neutral/secondary</code>, the title is <code>text/brand/primary</code> and the subtitle is <code>text/neutral/body</code>. The hero adds no colors of its own. It has no band color, which sets it apart from the <a href="/components/page-hero/">Page hero</a>.</p>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="use-h">
  <h2 id="use-h" class="type-h2">Using the case study hero</h2>
  <div class="rules">
    <div class="rule"><h3 class="type-h3">Do</h3><ul>
      <li>Use one at the top of a case study, with the page's one <code>h1</code> as the title.</li>
      <li>Give the image a text alternative that says what it shows.</li>
      <li>Put the width and height on the image so the page does not jump while it loads.</li>
      <li>Use the eyebrow for the type of project and the role.</li>
    </ul></div>
    <div class="rule"><h3 class="type-h3">Don't</h3><ul>
      <li>Use the buttons for links inside the site. They are secondary buttons that open a new tab.</li>
      <li>Use an image that is not 16:9. The hero crops it to 16:9, so the edges can be lost.</li>
      <li>Leave the alt text empty. The image carries content.</li>
    </ul></div>
  </div>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="a11y-h">
  <h2 id="a11y-h" class="type-h2">Accessibility</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The hero is a <code>&lt;header&gt;</code> with one <code>h1</code>.</li>
    <li>Each button that opens a new tab says so to a screen reader with the hidden text "(opens in new tab)", and shows the open-in-new icon.</li>
    <li>The back button is a link with a visible label, so the arrow is not the only signal.</li>
  </ul>
</section>
<section aria-labelledby="html-h">
  <h2 id="html-h" class="type-h2">The HTML</h2>
  <pre class="demo__code" style="padding:16px;overflow-x:auto;background:var(--arche-surface-brand-primary-subtle)" tabindex="0"><code>&lt;header class="cs-hero"&gt;
  &lt;div class="cs-hero__back"&gt;
    &lt;!-- tertiary button, arrow_back icon, "All work" --&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;div class="cs-hero__band"&gt;
    &lt;div class="cs-hero__text"&gt;
      &lt;div class="cs-hero__heading"&gt;
        &lt;p class="cs-hero__eyebrow type-label"&gt;Project type, Role&lt;/p&gt;
        &lt;h1 class="cs-hero__title type-h1"&gt;Case study title&lt;/h1&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;div class="cs-hero__lede"&gt;
        &lt;p class="cs-hero__subtitle type-lead"&gt;Subtitle.&lt;/p&gt;
        &lt;div class="cs-hero__actions"&gt;
          &lt;!-- secondary buttons, open_in_new icon, new tab --&gt;
        &lt;/div&gt;
      &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
    &lt;div class="cs-hero__image"&gt;
      &lt;img src="image.png" alt="What the image shows" width="2160" height="1215" fetchpriority="high"&gt;
    &lt;/div&gt;
  &lt;/div&gt;
&lt;/header&gt;</code></pre>
</section>
